@startuml strategic-architecture
' SPEC: _spec/apps/starchess/core/adjutant/strategic/strategic-architecture.puml
' purpose: ADJUTANT (SCRIPT STRATEGIC) — orchestrator layers on the naive base
' plus the known-vs-seen dials; which concerns are shipped and which naive
' concerns they substitute for.
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/ai/strategic/**
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/ai/context/index.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/__tests__/strategic/**
' see also: ../cc-focus.puml (which square the check weights aim at)
' see also: ../weight-ladder.puml (every value, and what a test pins)
' see also: strategic-economy.puml (the deploy dials in detail)
' see also: promotion-defense.puml (the enemy promotion race, in detail)
' see also: cc-retaliation.puml (the debt a shot on our own CC creates)
!include ../../../../../themes/proveo.puml

skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

title StarChess · Adjutant difficulty: ADJUTANT (SCRIPT STRATEGIC) — architecture

package "callers (the only ones)" {
  component "packages/starchess-arena\nplayers/strategic.ts\nheadless arena" as ARENA <<host>>
  component "apps/starchess\nscreens/SingleScreen.tsx\nopponent === ""strategic""" as APP <<host>>
  database "host-threaded kvs\nacross turns" as KVS <<db>>
  database "host-threaded ccIntel\nacross turns" as CCIN <<db>>
  database "host-threaded runnerMemory\nacross turns" as RMEM <<db>>
  database "host-threaded attackerMemory\nacross turns" as AMEM <<db>>
}

package "Strategic" {
  component "ai/strategic/orchestrator.ts\nstrategicCandidates · strategicAdjutant" as STRAT <<app>>
  component "ai/strategic/context.ts\nbuildStrategicCtx" as CTX <<app>>
  component "ai/strategic/intel.ts\nknown-vs-seen model" as INTEL <<app>>
  component "ai/strategic/runners.ts\nenemy promotion runners:\nfog-honest scan + ghost memory" as RUNI <<app>>
  component "ai/context/ccIntel.ts\ngetCCBestGuess — CC posterior" as CCI <<app>>
  component "ai/strategic/deployLookahead.ts\nhorizon 5 budget projection" as LOOK <<app>>
  package "ai/strategic/strategies" {
    component "economy\n**shipped**" as SSE <<app>>
    component "attackers\n**shipped** — no naive twin" as SSA <<app>>
    component "runners\n**shipped** — no naive twin" as SSR <<app>>
    component "threats\n**shipped**" as SST <<app>>
    component "checks\n**shipped**" as SSC <<app>>
  }
}

package "Naive base (unchanged — and now truly so)" {
  component "ai/context · ai/plans\nbuildAdjutantCtx + posture weights" as BASE <<app>>
  component "ai/strategies\nmapControl · captures · survival\n+ checks · threats (**substituted out**)" as NSTRAT <<app>>
}

package "Command (same as human)" {
  component "addScAction\nqueue-action + validation" as Q <<async>>
  database "ScFenSnapshot Q:" as SNAP <<db>>
}

ARENA ARROW_MAIN STRAT : snap in (opposite side) + storedFor
APP ARROW_MAIN STRAT : snap in (opponent side) + storedFor
ARENA ARROW_OPTIONAL KVS : kvs via ctx (absent → estimate)
ARENA ARROW_MAIN CCIN : ccIntel via SideContext → adjCtx
ARENA ARROW_MAIN RMEM : runnerMemory, same route
ARENA ARROW_MAIN AMEM : attackerMemory, same route
APP ARROW_MAIN AMEM : settledResolves cursor
APP ARROW_MAIN KVS : foldTracking, once per turn
APP ARROW_MAIN CCIN : foldTracking, once per turn
APP ARROW_MAIN RMEM : foldTracking, once per turn
STRAT ARROW_MAIN CTX : build once per turn
CTX ARROW_MAIN BASE : buildAdjutantCtx (read-only)
CTX ARROW_OPTIONAL INTEL : estimateKnownVsSeen\nwhen kvs absent
CTX ARROW_MAIN INTEL : cheesePromotion · winning\nfrom kvs
CTX ARROW_MAIN CCI : ccIntel from prior + vision + probe
CTX ARROW_MAIN RUNI : scanEnemyRunners (fog-honest)\n+ seek damp while one is urgent
RMEM ARROW_OPTIONAL RUNI : ghosts merged in as unseen runners
STRAT ARROW_MAIN SSA : score (attackers)
STRAT ARROW_MAIN SSR : score (runners)
SSE ARROW_OPTIONAL RUNI : runnerDeployValue on the deploy ring
STRAT ARROW_MAIN SSE : generate deploys (economy)
SSE ARROW_MAIN LOOK : bestDeploySequence(5)
SSE ARROW_OPTIONAL NSTRAT : reuse constants + deployPolicy
STRAT ARROW_MAIN SST : score (threats)
STRAT ARROW_MAIN SSC : score (checks)
STRAT ARROW_MAIN NSTRAT : score classical moves\nvia NAIVE_WITHOUT_CHECKS
STRAT ARROW_MAIN Q : commit chosen plan
Q ARROW_MAIN SNAP : gated write

note bottom of STRAT
  **Pattern:** Strategy → Command; same turn shape as naive.
  **Layering:** strategic = naive context + naive strategies, plus the
  known-vs-seen dials (""kvs"" / ""cheesePromotion"" / ""winning"") and the CC
  posterior (""ccIntel"").
  **Registry order is the tie-break order** — ""[economy, attackers, runners,
  captures, survival, threats, checks]"",
  economy first exactly as in naive; the final ranking sort is stable, so a
  plan proposed earlier wins an exact score tie.
  **Forbidden:** the pure core calling the engine, mutating the context, or
  bypassing ""addScAction"" gates.
end note

note as N_SUBST
  **The substitution — ""NAIVE_NOT_OVERRIDDEN"".** Classical-move scoring sums
  every source in ""SCORE_SOURCES"" = the seven strategic strategies plus the
  naive ones whose ""id"" no strategic strategy claims — which today leaves
  ""mapControl"" alone (""strategic/strategies/index.ts""):

  | concern | strategic | naive | scored by |
  | ""economy"" | shipped | kept | **both** — strategic generates deploys, naive constants are reused |
  | ""attackers"" | shipped | **none exists** | strategic only — the id lives in ""StrategicOnlyId"" |
  | ""runners"" | shipped | **none exists** | strategic only — the id lives in ""StrategicOnlyId"" |
  | ""threats"" | shipped | **filtered out** | strategic only |
  | ""checks"" | shipped | **filtered out** | strategic only |
  | ""captures"" | shipped | **filtered out** | strategic only |
  | ""survival"" | shipped (generate) | **filtered out** | strategic only — it reuses the naive ""score"" |
  | ""mapControl"" | not written | kept | naive only |

  ""StrategicOnlyId"" = ""runners | attackers"" — the two concerns with no naive
  counterpart at all, declared there rather than widening the naive
  ""StrategyId"" with an id the naive registry can never carry. The naive script
  reads promotion distance only about *our* marines (""NEAR_PROMOTE_RUSH""), so
  an enemy runner is invisible to it (""promotion-defense.puml""), and it keeps
  no record of who shot its Command Center (""cc-retaliation.puml"").

  The filter is what makes the fog contract enforceable: if both ""checks""
  strategies scored the same move, an omniscient naive weight would be added
  to a fog-honest strategic one and the guess branch would stop meaning
  anything. See ""../cc-focus.puml"".
end note

note as N_INVERSION
  **The import inversion is gone, so "Naive base (unchanged)" is true again.**
  ""ai/strategies/captures.ts"" used to import ""../strategic/context"" for a
  private deploy-defence predicate, which made the naive layer depend upward
  on the strategic one and quietly broke the layering this diagram claims.

  The predicate moved to ""board/deploy-reach.ts"", where both layers may read
  it, and the narrowing helpers it needed (""hasCcIntel"" · ""isStrategicCtx"")
  are deleted. The one field naive still wants is ""ctx.winning"", now an
  optional on ""AdjutantCtx"" that the strategic context populates and the naive
  build simply leaves absent — a declared hole rather than an ""in"" check on a
  type the layer is not supposed to know.
end note

STRAT .. N_SUBST
STRAT .. N_INVERSION

note as N_OPEN
  <color:#1A7F37>**RESOLVED — the script has an app consumer, and both hosts
  now thread all four folds.**</color> ""SingleScreen.tsx"" picks
  ""strategicAdjutant"" when the New Game modal's opponent is ""strategic"" and
  hands it ""kvs"" · ""ccIntel"" · ""runnerMemory"" · ""attackerMemory"". The first two
  come from ""foldTracking"" off the planning snapshot; the last two run off a
  ""settledResolves"" cursor, which is one fold per settled ply and the better
  cadence (""promotion-defense.puml""). The arena folds all four at its chip and
  settle points (""run/runMatch.ts""), and ""players/strategic.ts"" forwards every
  one of them into ""adjCtx"" — the ""ccIntel"" drop these diagrams used to record
  is fixed. The folds are one module, ""ai/strategic/tracking.ts"", in the core.

  <color:#CB2000>**OPEN — the Hoverbike probe channel is never fed.**</color>
  ""buildStrategicCtx"" and ""updateCcIntelForSnap"" both accept a
  ""lastProbe / lastCCProbe"" ("we sent a bike to ""e8"" and it was empty"), and
  ""players/strategic.ts:90"" forwards it — but **nothing anywhere writes one**:
  ""runMatch.ts"" builds ""SideContext"" without it and calls
  ""updateCcIntelForSnap(state, snap)"" with no probe argument, and
  ""SingleScreen"" does the same. So ""excluded"" grows only from what vision
  proves, and the half of the posterior that learns from a failed probe is
  dead in both hosts.

  **Planned, still unwired here:** periodic ""knownForTurn"" / gap persistence.
  The async engine enhancer *is* wired, but in the arena rather than in core —
  ""players/strategic.ts"" rescues candidate *scores* from an ""EngineFeed"" and
  never lets it decide legality (""_spec/packages/starchess-arena/arena.puml"").
end note

STRAT .. N_OPEN
@enduml
